        "original_id": "fa35a6c7-1728-5cbd-a171-07772e270499",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: North Midland Divisional Engineers, Allied forces, German forces\n- Events: World War II, Battle of France, Normandy landings, Rhine crossing\n- Places: France, Greece, Tunisia, Italy, Normandy, Belgium, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Western Front\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, the component units of the North Midland Divisional Engineers saw action in the Battle of France, in Greece, Tunisia, Italy, Normandy, and the Rhine crossing.\n- On 10 May 1940, the Battle of France began.\n- In six weeks from 10 May 1940, German forces defeated Allied forces by mobile operations.\n- In the same six-week campaign, German forces conquered France, Belgium, Luxembourg, and the Netherlands.\n- The Battle of France brought land operations on the Western Front to an end until 6 June 1944.",
